// `_self_` is the intra-package import prefix: "a module of the package this file belongs to",
// without naming the package.
//
// The subdirectory `para.db/` is the package `para/db` reached through a scope array, so its
// modules derive under the two-segment prefix `para.db` while its own root segment is `db`. Its
// files import each other as `use _self_.…` and the loader re-roots that leading segment to the
// whole prefix — the same source resolves standalone, where the prefix *is* `db`, and here.
//
// That is the property worth pinning: one spelling that survives being keyed anything by a
// consumer, and that does not have to change when the package is renamed.
// expect: stdout "[conn:rows] conn:rows"
// expect: exit 0
use para.db.nested.repo.all;
use para.db.query.run;

echo "${all()} ${run()}"
